rules.body:
Preserve configuration application before evaluating and writing the supplied record's parent fields, without inserting another suspension between these operations. Original src/record_editor.py: "        self._form.apply_config(config)
        self._form.write(
            {
                "parent_id": record["parent_id"],
                "parent_code": record["parent_code"],
                "parent_name": record["parent_name"],
            }
        )". Keep these values sourced from record rather than LOCAL_CONFIG.initial_values. This preserves existing evaluation order without assuming undocumented callback behavior.

Replace Personnel's remote request with src/config/personnel-form.json. Preserve asynchronous initialization completion and applicable error reporting: original src/editors/PersonnelEditor.vue contains "return getStaticConfig("personnel-form")" and ".catch((error) => {
          this.loadError = error.message;
        });". Preserve initialization on active mounting and later activation: "mounted() {
    if (this.active) this.getPageConfig();
  },
  watch: {
    active(next) {
      if (next) this.getPageConfig();
    },
  },".

Retain the imperative write of all three parent fields, alongside declarative defaults. Original src/editors/PersonnelEditor.vue contains "this.formApi.setValue({
            parentId: this.parentNode.id,
            parentCode: this.parentNode.code,
            parentName: this.parentNode.name,
          });". src/components/SchemaForm.vue implements "this.values = { ...this.values, ...values };
          this.imperativeWriteCount += 1;" separately from rule hydration's "this.ruleHydrationCount += 1;". Declarative hydration therefore cannot replace the imperative effect. Evaluate parentNode fields when applying configuration after readiness rather than capturing them before the wait.
